Best Practices for framework design

1. Avoid hardcoding values
2. Externalize test data
3. Use POM
4.Centralize reusable methods
5. Apply tags for grouping tests
6. Generate reports
7. Capture logs
8. CI/CD integration

We can mark a test with a tag like @smoke or @regression
and then run tests based on these tags using the command:
pytest -m "smoke"

We can also select tests based on test names using:
pytest -k "test_name" this will match any test with "test_name" in it.

We can run only failed tests using:
pytest --lf or pytest --last-failed

We can run tests in parallel using:
pytest -n 3 (where 3 is the number of parallel workers)
this is a part of pytest-xdist plugin

We can generate HTML reports using:
pytest --html=report.html (report.html is the name of the report file)
this is a part of pytest-html plugin




